    "text": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid deriving Cargo targets from nested test modules**\n\nWhen a PR edits a shared test helper or nested module such as `tests/support/mod.rs` or `tests/phase35_docs_doc_cli/missing_errors.rs`, this filter accepts it because the adapter glob includes `tests/**/*.rs`, then `_target_name` turns it into `mod`/`missing_errors` and the runner executes `cargo test --test <name>`. I checked `cargo test --help`: `--test <NAME>` selects a Cargo test target, and these nested module files are not standalone integration-test targets, so CI fails instead of falling back or running the owning tests whenever shared test code changes.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
